  "details": "## Description\n\nThe asterisks don't have any explained meaning, and the implied meaning of an asterisk indicating a \"required\" field is also not consistent. \"Category\" and \"Frequency\" have asterisks after the labels, but setting those fields is not required to submit a bug report (as demonstrated here).\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n1. Launch VRChat 2026.3.1 (OPEN BETA) build 1878 or later.\n\n2. Navigate to in-client bug reporting from Quick Menu - Report bug.\n\n3. Type in a single character to bug title, bug description and steps to reproduce. The \"Submit\" button will become active.\n\n4. Try submitting a bug report.\n\nSee the attached video from comments.\n\n## Details\n\n- Category: Audio\n\n- Frequency: Once\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.1-1881-ac10ed3a53-Release\n\nunityVersion: 2022.3.22f2-DWR\n\n---\n\n**Log file:** [output_log_2026-08-05_07-33-39.txt](https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/file/file_3c35b0b3-a703-4de8-a789-2a12c0a86c23/1/file)",
